CLASS:: ERBPhaseOctave
summary:: Auditory filterbank ERB phase-doubling octave-up pitch shifter
categories:: UGens>Pitch
related:: Guides/PitchShiftSuite, Classes/ERBSSBOctave, Classes/PVIntegerOctave, Classes/OCEANOctave

DESCRIPTION::
ERBPhaseOctave is an auditory filterbank pitch doubler based on Thuillier's ERB-PS2 technique. The input signal is split into 43 complex-valued Gammatone-like subbands spaced according to the human ear's Equivalent Rectangular Bandwidth (ERB) scale. Inside each subband, instantaneous analytic phase is doubled, transposing all subband content up by exactly one octave before resynthesis through the conjugate filterbank. This provides rich, analog-style polyphonic octave doubling.

Processing is monophonic; multichannel expansion applies over Arrays. Fixed nominal ratio of 2.0 (+1 octave).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio-rate mono input signal.

returns:: An audio-rate pitch-shifted signal.

EXAMPLES::

SUBSECTION:: Synthetic Signals

code::
// 1. Monophonic Sine: plays original (220 Hz) then pitch-shifted (fixed +1 octave)
(
fork {
    // Original
    x = {
        var sig = SinOsc.ar(220, 0, 0.1);
        sig * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
    2.1.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted
    x = {
        var sig = SinOsc.ar(220, 0, 0.1);
        var shifted = ERBPhaseOctave.ar(sig);
        shifted * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
};
)

// 2. Polyphonic Chord: plays original chord then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    // Original chord
    x = {
        var sig = Mix(SinOsc.ar([220, 277.18, 329.63], 0, 0.05));
        sig * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
    2.1.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted chord
    x = {
        var sig = Mix(SinOsc.ar([220, 277.18, 329.63], 0, 0.05));
        var shifted = ERBPhaseOctave.ar(sig);
        shifted * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
};
)

// 3. Percussive / Transient: plays original bursts then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    // Original bursts
    x = {
        var sig = PinkNoise.ar(0.1) * Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(4), 0.005, 0.15);
        sig * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
    2.1.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted bursts
    x = {
        var sig = PinkNoise.ar(0.1) * Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(4), 0.005, 0.15);
        var shifted = ERBPhaseOctave.ar(sig);
        shifted * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
};
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Recorded Audio

code::
// 4. Monophonic Recorded Sound (Guitar): original, then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    var buf = Buffer.read(s, Platform.userExtensionDir +/+ "PitchShiftSuite/HelpSource/Audio/PitchShiftSuite/guitar-monophonic.wav");
    s.sync;

    // Original
    x = { PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2) ! 2 }.play;
    buf.duration.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted
    x = {
        var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2);
        ERBPhaseOctave.ar(sig) ! 2;
    }.play;
    (buf.duration + 0.2).wait;

    buf.free;
};
)

// 5. Polyphonic Recorded Sound (Piano Chords): original, then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    var buf = Buffer.read(s, Platform.userExtensionDir +/+ "PitchShiftSuite/HelpSource/Audio/PitchShiftSuite/piano-polyphonic.wav");
    s.sync;

    // Original
    x = { PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2) ! 2 }.play;
    buf.duration.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted
    x = {
        var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2);
        ERBPhaseOctave.ar(sig) ! 2;
    }.play;
    (buf.duration + 0.2).wait;

    buf.free;
};
)
::
